From 07499b6189225a3d9911c6fe5cba7d445a9b4395 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Lando <gabriellando@hotmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:56:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Replace per-sample exp() with phasor recurrence in RX hot
 paths

sync_short and sync_long applied their frequency correction as
in[n] * exp(j*f*n), one sin/cos per sample. sync_short also copies a
fixed 540*80 samples after every detection, so at moderate frame density
most of the stream goes through that path. frame_equalizer did 64
exp() per OFDM symbol for the sampling-offset correction, 64 identical
exp(-beta), and interned "wifi_start" with pmt::string_to_symbol (global
lock) on every symbol.

Advance a phasor by one complex multiply per sample, re-anchored to the
exact exp() every 512 samples so float error cannot accumulate; hoist
the constant exp(-beta) and the interned symbol.

Offline throughput of the RX chain on a Ryzen 7 5700G, 802.11a BPSK 1/2
frames at 30% duty: 30.9 -> 75.9 MS/s; at 70% duty: 29.1 -> 67.1 MS/s.
Decoded frame counts are identical to the original, including at 6 dB
SNR with a 100 kHz carrier offset.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lib/frame_equalizer_impl.cc | 23 ++++++++++++++++-------
 lib/sync_long.cc            | 15 +++++++++++++--
 lib/sync_short.cc           | 13 ++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 41 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

