From 90ed62b9dabc96d90c9d01c80bb0bcfef8ff6e36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Lando <gabriellando@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:51:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add sync_short_fused: Schmidl-Cox front-end folded into
 sync_short

The examples wire sync_short behind a six-block Schmidl-Cox front-end
(delay, conjugate multiply, two moving averages, complex_to_mag, divide).
On quiet channels that chain costs more than the rest of the receiver,
mostly in scheduler handoffs between small blocks. sync_short_fused
computes the same autocorrelation and power inside one block with
sync_short's state machine. It takes the raw samples and produces the
same output and tags as the chain plus sync_short, so it is a drop-in
replacement; the original blocks are unchanged.

Offline throughput of the RX chain on a Ryzen 7 5700G, 802.11a BPSK 1/2
frames at 20 dB SNR (with the phasor patch):

  duty   original   phasor   phasor + sync_short_fused
   5 %   70.2       89.7     193.8 MS/s
  30 %   30.5       76.4     108.0 MS/s

Decoded frame counts are identical in all three.
